# MATLAB Development Rules

## Code Style
- lowerCamelCase for functions and variables, PascalCase for classes; name functions with a verb (`computeArea`)
- Descriptive names (`sampleRate`, not `sr`); named constants instead of magic numbers
- File name matches the primary function or class; terminate every function with `end`
- At most 6 positional inputs and 4 outputs per function
- Use `arguments` blocks for input validation (R2019b+), with `options.Name` for name-value arguments instead of `varargin`
- Keep functions under about 50 lines and nesting at 3 levels or fewer; move inner blocks into local functions
- End statements with semicolons to suppress output
- Do not name variables after built-in functions (`sum = 0` shadows `sum`)
- Build paths with `fullfile`, not hardcoded backslashes

## Modern APIs
- `readtable`, `readmatrix`, `writetable`, `writematrix` instead of `xlsread`, `csvread`, `dlmread`, `xlswrite`, `csvwrite`
- `datetime` instead of `datenum`, `datestr`, `now`
- String arrays (`"text"`) for text, `startsWith`/`matches`/`contains` instead of `strmatch`
- `dictionary` (R2022b+) instead of `containers.Map`
- Implicit expansion (`A - mean(A)`) instead of `bsxfun`
- `table`/`timetable` for data with named columns or timestamps
- `uifigure` components (`uibutton`, `uidropdown`) instead of `uicontrol`; App Designer instead of GUIDE (removed in R2025a)
- `exportgraphics` to save figures; `tiledlayout`/`nexttile` is preferred for multi-panel figures (`subplot` remains supported)
- `clearvars` instead of `clear all`

## Avoid
- `eval`, `evalc`, `evalin`, `assignin`: use dynamic field names `s.(name)`, function handles, or cell arrays
- `str2num` on external input without `Evaluation="restricted"` (R2022a+)
- Growing arrays inside loops: preallocate with `zeros(n, 1)` or similar

## Performance
- Vectorize element-wise loops; use logical indexing (`data(data > threshold)`) instead of `find` followed by indexing
- Most built-in functions (`sum`, `mean`, `filter`, `fft`) work column by column on matrices; do not loop over columns to call them
- Measure with `timeit` and profile before optimizing; do not add parallel code without a measurement
- Use `sparse` for large matrices that are mostly zeros

## Testing
- Class-based tests: `classdef computeAreaTest < matlab.unittest.TestCase`
- Arrange-act-assert, with no `if`, `for`, or `try` in test methods
- Verification methods: `verifyEqual`, `verifyError`, `verifySize`, `verifyWarning`
- Tolerances for floating point: `testCase.verifyEqual(actual, expected, AbsTol=1e-10)`
- Parameterized tests when only the data varies between cases
- Edge cases: empty, scalar, NaN, Inf, large arrays

## Error Handling
- Error identifiers in the form `"functionName:errorName"`
- `try`/`catch ME` with `ME.identifier` for specific handling
- `onCleanup` to close files and restore state when a function exits or errors

## Documentation
- H1 line: `%functionName - Brief description` (no period)
- Syntax paragraphs such as `%   Y = computeArea(X) computes...`, then an optional example and `%   See also` with related names
- Comment lines of 75 characters or fewer; no `%{ %}` block comments in help
- `%%` section breaks in scripts for the Live Editor

## File Organization
- One public function per file, plus local functions
- Group related functions in namespaces (`+namespaceName/` folders)
- Tests in `tests/`, examples in `examples/`
